{"kind":"request","text":"Ruling needed for the App-only private-read path under 3cfac8c2.\n\nI accept the existing Artroom Demo identifiers and will document that its key can mint for all 26 installation repositories; a one-repository installation remains the stronger operator choice. I will not read or copy that key. The planner owns its later transfer.\n\nThe current implementation uses an independent read credential for private GitHub lookup and Git reads. Its provider verifies repository name/stable ID before minting a write or member-read token. Removing the second static read token makes that pre-mint lookup unavailable for this private repository. Setting publicReads would not make private reads work.\n\nI propose an explicit opt-in installation-read mode, restricted to later-bound destinations with the exact operator pair. It would validate the configured App installation, mint a token for the one configured numeric repository ID with contents read only, validate the returned token's exact repository scope and permissions, then verify name/stable ID before any Git read. Write tokens remain one-ID contents write. Member read tokens remain one-ID contents read. No administration permission, broad-token fallback, static second token or change to the legacy independent-read path.\n\nPlease rule whether contents-read installation tokens are allowed as the narrower subset of your contents-write-only instruction. Also confirm that stable-ID/name verification after that already repository-ID-restricted read-token mint is acceptable for this mode. The exact register/full-destination/repository/branch check still precedes outside work. I will test missing repository-ID narrowing as a closed failure and add a distinguishing control.\n\nThe current third gate and Page CI continue at frozen b3da6de3f4; their result will remain evidence for those bytes. I will not send that head for source acceptance if it cannot run the approved witness configuration. Any production change for this ruling gets affected-owner checks and a fresh frozen gate.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on App-only private reads: one-ID contents-read installation tokens and stable-ID/name verification after that narrowed mint, with exact operator pair before outside work, or provide a different private-read mechanism. No key transfer or deployment before source and filled-configuration checker approval.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}